# SDK Extension HTML

Use React in this starter. Do not emit Ember, web-component, or `Ulx*` component syntax.

Start the widget document with these scripts in this order, then the application module:

```html
<script src="https://static.zohocdn.com/backstage/v1.0/javascript/sdk/ZSDK.min.js"></script>
<script src="https://static.zohocdn.com/backstage/v1.0/javascript/sdk/bs-frame-client.js"></script>
```

- Keep SDK URLs aligned with `src/config/project.config.js`.
- Use `<html class="h-full">`, `<body class="h-full m-0 ulx-default-mode">`, and a full-size `#root`.
- Do not link the legacy ULX editor stylesheet.
- Use PrimeReact for buttons, inputs, tables, dialogs, tags, and feedback.
- Compose layout with Tailwind utilities and token classes such as `bg-body`, `bg-surface`, `text-primary`, `border-border`, `flex`, `gap-*`, `p-*`, and `w-full`.
- Avoid custom CSS, inline styles, and hard-coded colors when a token class exists.
- Use semantic controls with labels and accessible names.
- Decorative icons use `aria-hidden="true"`; meaningful images have useful `alt` text.
- Render untrusted values as text; do not inject them through `innerHTML` or `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`.
